# A loop whose only choice is a "may", always declined, goes on for as long as its player declines. Bot2 has Fecundity
# ("Whenever a creature dies, that creature's controller may draw a card"). On turn 7 Bot1 animates its Entombed Worldgorger
# Dragon and the loop of the draw scenarios begins: each time Animate Dead's leaves ability sacrifices the Dragon,
# Fecundity's ability lets Bot1, its controller, draw a card, and Bot1 declines every time. The loop has an optional action
# in it, so it is no loop of mandatory actions (CR 104.4b's last sentence), and Bot1 is never made to take the draw (the
# engine never refuses a decline; docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-2): a person is held to the match clock, and the engine ends a
# game whose history reaches its limit in a draw (RX-1). The scenario sets that limit low; the game is a draw there, with
# Bot1's library as it was.

[Event Limit]
10000

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Worldgorger Dragon
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Forest
Fecundity
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Worldgorger Dragon)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fecundity.Cast
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Forest; Fecundity
? Bot1.Library.Count = 7
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Worldgorger Dragon)

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = EventLimit
Turn = 7
Step = Main1
Bot1.Library.Count = 7
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
